{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Pre-review cite audit against `aa37a738570` plus the in-flight corpus-move change (2026-10-27). The description's basis is `2e81cb9767c1`; main has moved well past it and **4 of 6 line-numbered cites no longer point at the cited construct**. Verified directly:\n\n| Description cite | Truth today |\n|---|---|\n| `heal.py:83` `UNRELIABLE_TITLE_PREFIX` | `:32` (`:273` is its only consumer) |\n| `heal.py:462` drift output | `:426` — `drift_path = repo_root / \".rebar\" / \"fixture_heal_drift.md\"` |\n| `_llm_eval_commands.py:136` cap `$25` | `:136` is still the right LINE but the cap is `cap_usd=25.0` inside `production_attempter(...)`, not a standalone constant — cite it as such |\n| `fixture_selection.py:71-99` override order | `:71` is a `repo_root: str` parameter. The packaged-fallback logic is around `:43,58,62` |\n| `docs/llm-framework.md:43-68` | `:43` is the \"Extras taxonomy\" heading — accurate |\n| `eval.py:58-75` | accurate (`eval_spec_path` docstring) |\n\n**Two substantive changes, not just line drift.**\n\n1. **The \"lists two extras\" premise is now wrong twice over.** The taxonomy section states \"The optional surface is **three** extras\", and `d279` (`disgusted-fretful-hare`, closed) has since registered a **fourth**, `evals`, in `rebar._optional.EXTRAS`. So the doc is stale against the code in a way this story must correct, and the AC should pin the count to what `EXTRAS` actually holds rather than to a literal. Note `tests/unit/test_optional.py` already iterates `EXTRAS`, so the count is checkable rather than asserted by hand.\n\n2. **`evals` is already registered — that half of the title is done.** `d279` added the `evals` extra, routed `genai_prices` through `guard_import`, and added the `evals:evals` spec to `.github/workflows/_optionality.yml`. This story's remaining work on that axis is DOCUMENTING it, not registering it. The title (\"register the evals extra\") should be re-scoped or the AC narrowed, otherwise the completion verifier is asked to confirm work that landed under a different ticket.\n\n**Also affected by the corpus move (`bafa`, in flight).** The description cites `docs/experiments/plan-review-gate/fixtures/drift-report.md` as the source of the 71 `fixture-drift:` tasks. That path becomes `evals/plan-review-gate/fixtures/drift-report.md`. Since the moved tree is frozen as authored, the file's own contents keep the old spelling, but this ticket's prose reference to it must be repointed — and the repo-wide grep in `bafa`'s AC2 does not cover ticket descriptions, so nothing will catch it automatically.\n\n**Process note for the revision.** `bafa` took six plan-review rounds, and every blocking finding but one was a hand-enumerated cite that had drifted or been missed. The durable fix there was to stop carrying a hand-kept worklist and define the target by a command the AC enforces. Worth applying the same shape here before the first review rather than after the fourth.\n\nThis ticket is not yet reviewable: it `depends_on` `bafa-2a33-6136-4fc5`, still `in_progress`, so `review-plan` fast-fails with no LLM until that closes."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793105066975629837,"uuid":"54a1660f-30bd-4be9-a504-f213e03ef65e"}